! conclusion: This is a problem-stating node: an AI-assisted estimate that tracks only time misses token cost, one that tracks only tokens misses human bottlenecks, and neither alone records uncertainty.

  + context: Minted by library-loop problem-authoring batch A4 from committed pattern history; it exists so effort-estimation mechanisms have a problem node to land on.

  + IF:
    Development work divides execution and judgment between agents and people.

  + HOWEVER:
    The problem, verbatim from the committed source: “Tracking only time misses token costs; tracking only tokens misses human bottlenecks; neither captures uncertainty”. (source: futon3 library/control/effort-estimation.flexiarg:14-15; introduced by commit 84c4045)

  + THEN:
    Treat this node as the landing point for @why edges from patterns that answer the two-resource estimation problem; solving it remains the mechanism pattern's work.

  + BECAUSE:
    A separate problem node preserves the source statement while making its rationale reachable in the library graph.

